#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader.md:105
msgid "Examine a window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader.md:107
msgid ""
"With the **Flat Review** feature, you can review the text and widgets of the "
"active window. In this mode, Orca treats the window as a two-dimensional "
"sheet of text. It browses the objects in the foreground, ignoring widget "
"hierarchy or other logical grouping within the window. It can't access "
"window elements that are currently off-screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader.md:109
msgid ""
"You can navigate the \"flattened\" content by line, by word, by character, "
"and by object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader.md:111
msgid ""
"When you enter Flat Review mode, it captures the state of the window at that "
"moment. If the content of the window changes, Flat Review doesn't update "
"automatically. You can refresh the Flat Review context by toggling Flat "
"Review off and back on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/navigate-the-screen-using-the-screen-reader.md:113
msgid ""
"If you use the application's navigation commands to move the caret or to "
"give focus to another object, you automatically leave Flat Review."
msgstr ""

